      "writtenOn": "2023-09-29T22:23:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This seems odd since it is the only case here that is not used at all by the GKI build - it is for vendor builds.\n\nWould it make more sense to go ahead and add `GKI_HIDDEN_DRM_MODULE_CONFIGS\u003dm` to gki_defconfig to build as a GKI module? If partners are modifying, we can make it an unprotected GKI module.",
      "revId": "ece222967c4fbde897f557f33fefbfe844ecc70d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f1769fb3_15d57f93",
        "filename": "init/Kconfig.gki",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 16,
      "author": {
        "id": 1557540
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-29T22:35:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m okay with making them unprotected GKI modules. I didn\u0027t add this to the `gki_defconfig` because @gregkh@google.com made a point in the past about not wanting to add `CONFIG_CFG80211\u003dm` in favor of just having partners add it to their own defconfig fragments if they want it. I\u0027m fine with either way.",
      "parentUuid": "104c4b69_6fcb2169",
      "revId": "ece222967c4fbde897f557f33fefbfe844ecc70d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d0aa970c_2e18d6e5",
        "filename": "init/Kconfig.gki",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 16,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-29T22:44:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How are partners using these today? If they have a vendor module that depends on it, it seems like they can add a `select DRM_DISPLAY_DP_HELPER` to cause them to be built. Can you add more detail to \"partners can\u0027t build them as modules without modifying the GKI source code\"?",
      "parentUuid": "f1769fb3_15d57f93",
      "revId": "ece222967c4fbde897f557f33fefbfe844ecc70d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4879d08c_090ba2ed",
        "filename": "init/Kconfig.gki",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 16,
      "author": {
        "id": 1557540
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-30T00:24:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Normally vendors don\u0027t use Kconfigs for their OOT drivers. They just set the configs using KBUILD_OPTIONS which doesn\u0027t allow you to build drivers outside of your OOT repo. Fortunately we actually do support external Kconfig files using KCONFIG_EXT_PREFIX. So I went ahead and tested this out by adding a Kconfig file to the OOT DRM driver with:\n```\nselect DRM_DISPLAY_DP_HELPER\nselect DRM_DISPLAY_HELPER\n```\nand it\u0027s working now. So I\u0027ll abandon this change for now and push for that solution.",
      "parentUuid": "d0aa970c_2e18d6e5",
      "revId": "ece222967c4fbde897f557f33fefbfe844ecc70d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
  ],
